\section{Testing}
\label{sec:enrich-testing}

Tests are distributed throughout this document after each function.
The test file collects all test chunks.

The autouse fixture disables the preprint fallback's real lookup: the
fallback lives in its own module ([[scholar.preprint]]) with its own
clients, so the [[scholar.enrich.get_provider]] patches these tests
use would not reach it, and a test paper without a PDF would trigger
live OpenAlex and Crossref requests.  Tests of the fallback wiring
patch [[find_preprint]] again themselves, overriding the fixture.

A second autouse fixture does the same for the enrichment providers.
Most tests patch [[scholar.enrich.get_provider]] with a mock, but a test
that exercises enrichment only indirectly does not: fetching references
and citations enriches every fetched paper by DOI, so
[[TestEnrichmentCache]] used to send real DOI lookups to every provider
in [[ENRICHMENT_PROVIDERS]]---with the developer's keys, when set.
By default, therefore, no provider is configured (the same answer
[[get_provider]] gives for an unknown name), and a test that wants
enrichment to find something says so with its own patch, which takes
precedence over the fixture.
The abstract services, Crossref and Europe PMC, are not providers and
are not reached through [[get_provider]] (\cref{sec:enrichment-providers}),
so the fixture switches off [[abstract_source]] as well; otherwise
every test that patches [[get_provider]] and enriches a paper without
an abstract in the default order would ask them.
The suite-wide network guard [[block_network]]
(\cref{sec:test-configuration}) would catch such a leak too, by failing
the test; this fixture is what keeps the leak from happening.

