\section{Batch Enrichment}

For enriching multiple papers (e.g., after a search), we provide a batch
function with optional progress reporting.

Before its loop, the batch function lets OpenAlex answer the whole
batch's DOIs in a few requests ([[prefetch_dois]],
\cref{sec:openalex-doi-batch}), fifty DOIs to a request instead of one.
The loop itself is unchanged: when [[enrich_paper]] reaches OpenAlex
for a paper, the answer is already in the cache.
We prefetch only when OpenAlex is among the providers the loop will
try (and has the method), and only the DOIs of papers that
[[needs_enrichment]] for the requested fields, since the loop asks
no provider about the others.
A paper without a DOI is included under the arXiv DOI derived from its
URL, because [[enrich_paper]] derives that DOI before its lookups too.

The prefetch is not free when a provider earlier in the order fills
a paper first: the batch has then asked OpenAlex about a DOI the loop
never needed it for.
That costs one fiftieth of a request per such paper.
In money the trade is the other way round: the [[endpoint_costs_usd]]
that OpenAlex's rate-limit report gave on 2026-11-18 (quoted in
\url{https://github.com/dbosk/scholarcli/issues/138}) price a list
request at \$0.0001 and a single-work lookup at nothing, so the batch
spends a little budget to save requests and time.
It also says what the fast path is.
Semantic Scholar comes first in [[ENRICHMENT_PROVIDERS]], and without
a key its declared rate is one request every three seconds
([[SemanticScholarProvider.LIMITS]]), so a paper that Semantic Scholar
answers still costs three seconds whatever OpenAlex holds.
The batch saves time only for papers that reach OpenAlex, and saves
the most when OpenAlex is asked first:
[[--enrich-providers openalex,s2,...]].

<<enrichment functions>>=
def _prefetch_openalex_lookups(
    papers: list[Paper],
    fields: list[str],
    providers: list[str] | None,
) -> None:
    """Batch the OpenAlex DOI lookups that enriching `papers` will make."""
    if "openalex" not in (providers or ENRICHMENT_PROVIDERS):
        return
    provider = get_provider("openalex")
    prefetch = getattr(provider, "prefetch_dois", None)
    if prefetch is None:
        return
    dois = [
        paper.doi or derive_arxiv_doi(paper)
        for paper in papers
        if needs_enrichment(paper, fields)
    ]
    prefetch([doi for doi in dois if doi])
